 "rule_text": "Dev data = office_loop only (473 frames, TUM never used). K = keyframes of the upstream LK selector (min_disparity 50). P_adj = consecutive keyframe pairs (cap 60, evenly spaced). P_loop = for each keyframe in the last ceil(15%) of K, the keyframe in the first ceil(15%) of K with the smallest SALAD L2 distance (upstream ImageRetrieval on the VGGT-loader frames, i.e. the solver's own retrieval). N = pairs whose index gap is within [0.30, 0.70] x len(K), 60 pairs by an even deterministic stride over the lexicographically sorted candidates. Raw image_match_ratio from a 2-frame forward with the later (query) frame first, as the solver does. VGGT at its upstream setting, Omega at every global inter-frame block in {12,13,15,16,17,18,19,21,22,23}. L* = argmax ROC AUC of (P_adj U P_loop) vs N, ties -> layer closest to 20 (then the lower layer). FAR_vggt = fraction of N with VGGT raw ratio >= 0.95. tau = (1 - FAR_vggt) quantile (numpy linear interpolation) of Omega raw ratios on N at L*; FAR_vggt == 0 -> tau = max(Omega N ratios) + 1e-6. A loop closure passes when raw >= threshold (upstream rejects raw < threshold). Note on the VGGT layer: the rule text named layer 20, the Aggregator default, but main.py builds VGGT() whose constructor passes target_layer=21 to the Aggregator, so the upstream operating point is layer 21. FAR_vggt is taken at layer 21 and reported at layer 20 as well.",
